    "note": "Polish mirror of the 24-item probe. The English half is byte-identical to data/tasks_time_v2.json, so English acts as the same within-item ceiling in both files and the two can be pooled. The Polish half is the crossed design: Polish counts INTO the coming hour for «wpół do X» (07:30 = wpół do ósmej) and FROM the completed hour for «kwadrans po X» and «N po X» (07:20 = dwadzieścia po siódmej). Russian counts into the hour for all three. So `pl_direction` splits the same clock times by construction inside one language. Prediction from the memorisation reading: Polish `into_hour` behaves like Russian and Polish `from_hour` behaves like English. The rival reading, that models are simply worse at Slavic or at lower-resource languages, predicts both Polish cells fail. WORDING NOT YET CHECKED BY A NATIVE SPEAKER — see tools/make_polish_probe.py."
